WEBVTT

00:00:14.259 --> 00:00:16.420
I know hunting Dan's owners is your top priority,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.940
but if you haven't found anything in South America,

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.019
we still have a situation back here in Kansas

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:23.519
we need to deal with.

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:26.379
No, he'll be here in 15 minutes.

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:31.210
Okay, great, see in a few.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.090
Dr. Caselli, you're early.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.750
You are annoyingly persistent, Miss Sullivan.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.289
I've already told you I don't know anything.

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:42.109
Don't sell yourself short, doctor.

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:44.810
I think you're a very knowledgeable man.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.609
In the last few months, over a dozen patients

00:00:46.609 --> 00:00:48.289
have been transferred out of the high security wing

00:00:48.289 --> 00:00:50.969
at Bel-Riv, and I believe that's your signature

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:54.799
on all the paperwork.

00:00:54.799 --> 00:00:57.439
Patients are transferred in and out of mental facilities

00:00:57.439 --> 00:00:59.780
all the time.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.600
Even ones that exhibit unusual abilities?

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.280
Where are they transferred to?

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.719
Is Luther Corp involved?

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:13.159
Does this have anything to do with 33.1?

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:15.000
I'll take that as a no comment.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.329
I didn't want any of this.

00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:27.349
So much money.

00:01:27.349 --> 00:01:28.890
Chloe, you okay?

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.890
Yeah.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.170
Just the nick time, as always.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.510
It wasn't me. He was already down when I got here.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:35.510
What?

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:37.510
If it wasn't you, then...

00:01:37.510 --> 00:02:22.319
Still too slow, stretch?

00:02:22.319 --> 00:03:26.659
I thought you were the fastest man alive.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:29.659
Whoever he was, he saved your life, which is more than I can say.

00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:31.659
Oh, come on, Clark. It wasn't your fault.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:34.659
I mean, even with all your powers, you can't be everywhere at once.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:35.659
Oh, I have to be.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:38.159
I'm the only one who can round up the prisoners from the Phantom Zone

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:40.659
and stop Lex from experimenting on people with abilities.

00:03:40.659 --> 00:03:43.659
What'd you find out from Casseli about 33.1?

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:44.659
Nothing, and I'm not going to.

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:45.659
I'm going to.

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:49.159
Casselli was in and out of prison before the ink could dry on his fingerprints.

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:50.159
How'd he get out so fast?

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:54.159
I don't know, but a Luther Corp lawyer paid Cicely a visit right before his release.

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:55.159
Lex.

00:03:55.159 --> 00:03:57.159
Cassellie could be stashed halfway around the world by now.

00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:59.159
I'll get in touch with Lionel.

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:00.159
Maybe he can tell us something.

00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:02.159
I'll keep sifting through my Luther Corp Intel.

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:05.159
Maybe we'll get lucky, and I'll come up with a feed-like promise.

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:06.159
Hey, Gorgeous.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:07.159
What's up?

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:08.159
You missed me?

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:09.159
I'm Bart Allen.

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:11.159
We had a moment in talent last time I was here.

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:14.159
Two years ago, before you had a boyfriend.

00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:17.660
Oh, right, wow. It's good to see you again, Bart.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:23.649
Yeah, well, the pleasure's all mine, senorita.

00:04:23.649 --> 00:04:24.649
See around.

00:04:24.649 --> 00:04:31.029
No, caliente.

00:04:31.029 --> 00:04:32.029
Knock it off.

00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:33.529
What's with the Spanish?

00:04:33.529 --> 00:04:36.029
Whoa, I just grabbed lunch down in Mexico, man.

00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:38.529
They got this burrito down there, Ellen Testino Buster.

00:04:38.529 --> 00:04:41.029
Got to take a run down there with me to try one.

00:04:41.029 --> 00:04:43.529
What are you doing here, Bart?

00:04:43.529 --> 00:04:47.029
What? I'm hanging out with my Amigo, man. What's the look like?

00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:49.029
That's what I'm trying to find out.

00:04:49.029 --> 00:04:51.529
Last time you blew through town, you stole my dad's wallet.

00:04:51.529 --> 00:04:53.529
Then swipe to prize this artifact from Lex.

00:04:53.529 --> 00:04:55.029
You nearly got yourself killed.

00:04:55.029 --> 00:04:57.529
Yeah, yeah, those are the days, huh?

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:58.529
Yeah, all right.

00:04:58.529 --> 00:05:00.529
Look, ma'am.

00:05:00.529 --> 00:05:03.529
I already told you things are different now, okay?

00:05:03.529 --> 00:05:06.529
I mean, back then, I needed a super kick in the butt,

00:05:06.529 --> 00:05:07.529
and you laid it on me.

00:05:07.529 --> 00:05:10.529
And ever since then, there's been no more stealing for this gringo, I swear.

00:05:10.529 --> 00:05:12.529
Am I really supposed to just buy that?

00:05:12.529 --> 00:05:14.529
Well, I could squirt out some tears for that, I'll help.

00:05:14.529 --> 00:05:16.529
No, but the truth might.

00:05:16.529 --> 00:05:18.529
What were you doing at the Daily Planet?

00:05:18.529 --> 00:05:21.529
I saw Chloe Alicia's at a byline while back, and I saw,

00:05:21.529 --> 00:05:24.529
I was in town on business, figured I had to check it out.

00:05:24.529 --> 00:05:25.529
What kind of business?

00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:27.529
I'm a courier.

00:05:27.529 --> 00:05:30.529
Pick things up, I drop them off, lickety split, don't have a fit.

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:36.250
Look, man, whatever. You don't trust me, it's fine.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:40.250
Okay, I'll be gone before you can even blink.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:45.399
I don't know. I can still blink pretty fast.

00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:47.399
Mexico, huh?

00:05:47.399 --> 00:05:49.399
You want to go get that burrito?

00:05:49.399 --> 00:06:06.160
Excellente.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:09.160
That is what I call the three martini lunch.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.160
It's a four martini lunch.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:15.160
If you include the one that you spelled out my shirt.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.160
Right.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.160
Yeah.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.160
Well, how am I ever going to make it up to you?

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.160
I don't know.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:27.160
Because, uh, it's my favorite shirt.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:33.160
Well, then I think we should get into the laundry so that it doesn't stay.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:51.569
Yeah, that's a good idea.

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:52.569
I get it.

00:06:52.569 --> 00:07:05.100
Go ahead. Give me five minutes.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.529
I, uh...

00:07:08.529 --> 00:07:14.529
You know, what I had in mind is going to take a little longer than five minutes.

00:07:14.529 --> 00:07:19.990
Brain check?

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:20.990
Sure.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:24.990
I'll just put it next to the rest of the umbrellas you keep handing me.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.269
Lois.

00:07:27.269 --> 00:07:36.379
I mean, is it just me, or is this relationship all interrupt us and no coitus?

00:07:36.379 --> 00:07:39.379
You're always running off just when things start getting interesting.

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:43.379
And I like being interested, a lot.

00:07:43.379 --> 00:07:46.879
Yeah, no, you're right.

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:51.050
It's, uh, it's not fair to you.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:57.819
I think we should take a break.

00:07:57.819 --> 00:08:03.850
You mean, like, what?

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.850
See other people?

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.850
Uh, well, okay, yeah.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.850
I mean, if that's, you know, what you want,

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.850
I was actually thinking more along the lines of taking a vacation.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:19.439
Together.

00:08:19.439 --> 00:08:20.439
Really?

00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:21.439
Yeah, really.

00:08:21.439 --> 00:08:26.360
No rushing out in the middle of the good stuff?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.360
No. None.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.360
It'll be you, me, and, and...

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.360
And...

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.360
Moni Carlo?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.360
Hmm.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.360
This is just a few things that I do need to take care of before we go.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.360
And I think once we get...

00:08:38.360 --> 00:09:13.740
I'll start packing.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:14.740
I need to talk to you.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.740
You alone?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.740
Just me and my shadow, Dad.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.740
Honest in Paris with Nell.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.740
Shopping for a wedding dress.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:27.200
That's good. She's out of the country, considering what's happening.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.200
Look, if this is about Dr. Casella...

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.200
Casseli, he's the least of our worries.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.200
Another Luther Corp facility has been hit.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.200
That's six.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.200
Each one of them has some connection with 33.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.200
The only thing housed in those facilities was peripheral research.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.200
All the vital data is still secure in the mainframe.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.200
And how long do you think before that location is compromised?

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:52.200
If it ever became public that Luther Corp is experimenting on people with abilities...

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.200
It won't.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.200
What's this?

00:09:55.200 --> 00:10:00.610
A single frame pulled up a security camera from one of the break-ins.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:12.629
Whoever is responsible has the ability to move faster than a speeding bullet.

00:10:12.629 --> 00:10:18.629
Such a unique individual making an interesting test subject to add to 33.1.

00:10:18.629 --> 00:10:19.629
Don't you think?

00:10:19.629 --> 00:10:23.519
What do you plan to do?

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:25.519
Protect our investment.

00:10:25.519 --> 00:10:27.519
Come on, I'll walk you out.

00:10:27.519 --> 00:10:59.980
Yeah, I got it.

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:01.980
Me and meet the rendezvous.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:19.789
I'm in the shadows all night.

00:11:19.789 --> 00:11:23.710
Just being careful.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:26.710
After all, I'm not as fast as you.

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:46.309
Clark.

00:11:46.309 --> 00:11:49.309
I was just thinking about you.

00:11:49.309 --> 00:11:50.309
Just thinking about you...

00:11:50.309 --> 00:11:52.309
You got a funny way of showing it.

00:11:52.309 --> 00:11:54.309
I've left you half a dozen messages.

00:11:54.309 --> 00:11:56.309
I'm sorry, I've been preoccupied.

00:11:56.309 --> 00:11:59.309
Helping that doctor from Bel-Rive get out of jail.

00:11:59.309 --> 00:12:04.559
Clark, my involvement with Bel-Rive is past history.

00:12:04.559 --> 00:12:10.559
But it appears that you still have a very active interest in breaking into Luther Corp.

00:12:10.559 --> 00:12:16.909
Where is this taken?

00:12:16.909 --> 00:12:17.909
Mexico.

00:12:17.909 --> 00:12:20.909
The Luther Corp processing plan.

00:12:20.909 --> 00:12:26.120
If you're going to continue playing games like this...

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.120
You should be more careful.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:31.120
This isn't me.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:44.070
No? Who is it then?

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.070
God, Mr. Kay, thanks you so much. This is so good.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:49.070
Where do you put it all?

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:51.070
You eat more than Clark and he's twice your size.

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:55.070
Yeah. Well, you know, I burn a lot of calories.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:59.070
Well, there's plenty more in the fridge. Um, I have to run to a meeting.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.070
Oh, would you mind cleaning up?

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:06.169
Yeah, anything for you, Mrs. Kay.

00:13:06.169 --> 00:13:08.169
It's nice to have you here.

00:13:08.169 --> 00:13:09.669
It's nice to have you here, Bart.

00:13:09.669 --> 00:13:11.169
I hope you stay longer this time.

00:13:11.169 --> 00:13:19.460
Hey, what's up, man?

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.960
You just missed the killer spread.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.460
You can cut the act.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.460
I know about Luther Corp.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:27.929
And the break-ins by somebody who's as fast as me.

00:13:27.929 --> 00:13:28.929
Yeah, fast.

00:13:28.929 --> 00:13:29.929
Actually.

00:13:29.929 --> 00:13:32.429
You know, it's funny, I actually believe you a little story

00:13:32.429 --> 00:13:33.929
about how it changed your life.

00:13:33.929 --> 00:13:35.929
Look, it's not a story, Clark, okay?

00:13:35.929 --> 00:13:37.929
I'm not the same guy.

00:13:37.929 --> 00:13:40.429
You stole it from Lex before, you're stealing from him again.

00:13:40.429 --> 00:13:41.929
What's the difference?

00:13:41.929 --> 00:13:42.929
It's just, it's...

00:13:42.929 --> 00:13:43.929
It's complicated.

00:13:43.929 --> 00:13:45.429
I'm a smart guy, explain it to me.

00:13:45.429 --> 00:13:45.929
I can't.

00:13:45.929 --> 00:13:48.929
Why not? I thought we were amigos.

00:13:48.929 --> 00:13:50.929
You know what we are.

00:13:50.929 --> 00:13:53.929
Then tell me why you're stealing from Luther Corp.

00:13:53.929 --> 00:14:01.460
I can't.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:12.480
I'll find out for myself, then.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:15.480
Look, I'm sorry, I can't tell you all my secrets, Clark.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:31.639
Okay, I thought a guy like you would understand it.

00:14:31.639 --> 00:14:32.639
I know, it's just a vacation.

00:14:32.639 --> 00:14:33.639
What?

00:14:33.639 --> 00:14:35.639
Vacation? No, vacation is Palm Springs.

00:14:35.639 --> 00:14:38.639
Monte Carlo is a fairy tale.

00:14:38.639 --> 00:14:41.639
Yeah, hopefully without Prince Charming,

00:14:41.639 --> 00:14:43.639
having a disappearing actor,

00:14:43.639 --> 00:14:45.639
Five minutes.

00:14:45.639 --> 00:14:49.639
Um, I think you'll be keeping his full attention, Lois.

00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:50.639
Yeah, you know, I'd better.

00:14:50.639 --> 00:14:56.200
It's not like I go Victoria's secret for anybody.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.200
What do you think, though?

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.200
Should I've gone with a black blaze?

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.200
No.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:02.200
Something tells me green is definitely his color.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.200
Hey, Chloe.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:06.580
God, Smallville.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:07.580
Learn how to knock.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.580
What if I'd been naked?

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.580
Ew.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:14.580
Lois is jetting off to Monte Carlo with Oliver.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.580
Oliver?

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:17.580
Yeah, I'll send you a postcard.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:18.580
I'm not too busy.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.580
No, Lois, you should, um...

00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.580
Get a couple new bikinis.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.580
Good idea.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.580
Thanks, Smallville.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:34.220
Maybe it wasn't such a good idea to help Oliver keep his secret from that.

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:36.220
What? That he's the green arrow?

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:39.220
No offense, Clark, but she weren't exactly honest with Lana about your secret either.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.720
Look how that ended up.

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:46.720
Maybe all keeping secrets does sometimes is force you to lie to the people you care about.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:54.860
Are we still talking about Oliver?

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:58.240
The guy who saved you at the planet?

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.240
He didn't exactly get away.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.240
It's Bart.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.240
What?

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:03.240
Wait a minute.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.240
Bart can super speed, too?

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.240
He's actually a lot faster than I am.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.240
That's the truth.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.240
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.240
It's fine.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:10.240
You were protecting him. It's okay.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.240
I mean, if anyone gets it, it's me.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.240
But why are you outing him now?

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.240
I think he's headed for trouble, and I need to find him.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.240
Can you GPS his cell phone?

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.240
Yeah, I can try. Do you have his number?

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:23.240
He broke into a Luther Court plant down in Mexico.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:24.240
Now I think Lex is on to him.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:26.240
If he tries to break into another facility...

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:30.240
No good. His phone must be off.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.240
What about call history?

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:32.240
Can you pull up a record?

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.240
Legally?

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:34.240
Absolutely not.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:45.379
Silver dozen calls of that number in the last 24 hours.

00:16:45.379 --> 00:16:49.740
Let's see who's on the other end?

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.740
Artemis Global Consortium?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:56.820
Never heard of them.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:17:01.820
It's a subsidiary of Jail International, which is a satellite company currently orbiting...

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:04.819
Queen Industries.

00:17:04.819 --> 00:17:07.819
It's all in her.

00:17:07.819 --> 00:17:09.819
He's using Bart to attack Luther Corp.

00:17:09.819 --> 00:17:17.470
I'm in.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:50.099
Not so fast now, are you?

00:17:50.099 --> 00:18:03.539
Oh.

00:18:03.539 --> 00:18:08.500
Clark, whatever's got your tidy whitties in a bunch.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:09.500
Now's not the time.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.500
Where's Bart?

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.500
I saw his phone records.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.500
I know he's working for you.

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.500
Not for me.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.500
Working with me.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.500
There's a difference.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.500
It's not gonna matter when he ends up in jail.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.500
Or worse.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:23.500
Yeah, you don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.500
